# kotlin hex: decoding as a declarative binding of the hex shim's own expression (decision 132 of
# term/self-host/change/001): two UTF-16 units at a time, each read as a base-16 number, so a pair that is not hex
# raises NumberFormatException as the shim did. Encoding stays in the linked hex runtime shim: its Term version
# (task/term/shim-bench/kotlin/hex.candidate.tree) read over 1.2 on two runs (kotlin/hex.baseline.json). Internal:
# reached only through the public hex API.

dock load
  load <global:hex>, name hex

task to-hex
  take input, like text
  like text
  send back
    call hex/encode
      read input

bind from-hex
  take input, like text
  like text
  case kotlin
    text <String(($input).chunked(2).map \{ it.toInt(16).toByte() \}.toByteArray(), Charsets.UTF_8)>
